Hi Efrain,

I came across TSM Collision while looking at body shops in Temecula, and your=
 work and reputation genuinely stand out - the paint detail, and the way cust=
omers talk about how you keep them informed, is exactly what a great shop sho=
uld be.

That's actually why I reached out. All of that quality is a little hard to fi=
nd online: every new job has to come in by phone during business hours, so ni=
ghts and weekends go to voicemail (and usually to whoever picks up next), and=
 a shop down the street with worse work has a much bigger wall of reviews tha=
n you do. The cars are better; the scoreboard just doesn't show it yet.

I put together a short proposal with three ways we could fix that, smallest t=
o largest:

1. AI Phone Receptionist - answers every call 24/7, captures the lead, and bo=
oks estimate requests so you stop losing after-hours jobs.
2. Full Shop Automation - the phone agent plus automatic repair-status texts,=
 a review-request engine, online booking, and lead follow-up (built to work a=
longside your CCC ONE).
3. Full Growth Partner - all of that plus website, local SEO, ads, and an on-=
site AI agent.

Everything is done-for-you and month-to-month - no long contract, and support=
 is included Monday through Friday. The full breakdown and pricing are in the=
 attached PDF.

Would you be open to a quick 10-15 minute call this week so I can walk you th=
rough it? Happy to work around your schedule.

Best,
Leo Lebel
